00:34:33.390 --> 00:34:34.546
This is what would happen.

00:34:34.546 --> 00:34:35.615
And there are coincidences.

00:34:35.615 --> 00:34:37.308
1/m,

00:34:37.308 --> 00:34:38.859
1/(m^2)

00:34:40.873 --> 00:34:45.079
So these coefficients are correctly found.

00:34:45.079 --> 00:34:47.349
m1 is additionally hidden here.

00:34:47.349 --> 00:34:51.902
So don't pay attention to the fact that there is a square here, and here it's just m.

00:34:51.902 --> 00:34:53.268
13, 13

00:34:53.268 --> 00:34:54.627
3, 3

00:34:54.627 --> 00:34:55.841
1, 1

00:34:55.841 --> 00:34:56.706
6, 6

00:34:56.706 --> 00:34:58.914
Everything matches. Perfect.

00:35:00.534 --> 00:35:06.303
With Sin[x]^2 there is a variable "a".

00:35:11.120 --> 00:35:14.851
This two matches.

00:35:14.851 --> 00:35:20.000
But with x^2 it's not so straightforward.

00:35:24.029 --> 00:35:25.726
Alright.

00:35:25.726 --> 00:35:30.000
Now let's look at the quality of the approximation.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.998
Just sin minus one divided by the sum.

00:35:33.998 --> 00:35:39.037
And here are these new approximation variants that we got.

00:35:39.037 --> 00:35:43.739
And these polynomials no longer contain sines.

00:35:43.739 --> 00:35:48.083
Everything is already calculated here.

00:35:48.083 --> 00:35:50.834
Let's try.

00:35:50.834 --> 00:35:56.114
The blue plot - the first approximation.

00:35:56.114 --> 00:36:01.778
The yellow plot - we took m1^2.

00:36:01.778 --> 00:36:07.675
Essentially, we took the component with m1^2 in the denominator.

00:36:07.675 --> 00:36:12.329
And here we took the component with m1^3 in the denominator.

00:36:12.329 --> 00:36:14.151
This is m1.

00:36:14.151 --> 00:36:16.263
Here is m1^2.

00:36:16.263 --> 00:36:20.000
And we got the blue plot.

00:36:20.000 --> 00:36:28.032
The difference is a small number, 0.0005, but we can do better.

00:36:28.032 --> 00:36:29.310
Where is our yellow plot?

00:36:29.310 --> 00:36:32.098
Here it is, finally born.

00:36:32.098 --> 00:36:36.289
2 * 10^-9.

00:36:36.289 --> 00:36:42.407
And the green plot is 2 * 10^-11.

00:36:42.407 --> 00:36:47.138
These are the different levels of approximation.

00:36:47.138 --> 00:36:48.946
So, what do we have?

00:36:48.946 --> 00:36:51.154
By summing up 20 terms,

00:36:51.154 --> 00:36:54.730
or more precisely, 20 on the left, 20 on the right,

00:36:54.730 --> 00:37:04.308
